[gd_scene format=3]

; The Slag, east of the Kiln (map offset (170, -126)): the volcanic layer's hub, a cavern over a river of slag. Platforms
; of basalt step across the river (falling in is the end: the slag swallows the pilgrim, even plated); heat rises from it
; between them. A shrine on the middle platform, under the vent of the Chimney (ledges climb to it: the shortcut home to
; the Coldstacks). West, the Kiln; east, the Ashfall. Two ways down: a pool of coolant west of the river whose bottom
; opens on the Quench (Ballast), and a cracked plug in the eastern platform over the Basalt (the Drill's dive).

